## Linking CIL objects into a PE (ImplementationPlan.md M20; 5.9.4, 5.9.7,
## 5.9.10, 5.9.12; 5.7.10 for the listings). Two objects that llc writes with
## -filetype=obj (the writer clang -c uses, M19) and an import library link
## into an EXE with no ilasm:
## - the image is an IL-only PE32+ EXE for the triple's machine with
##   '<msil>Main' as its entry point, no COFF symbol table, the Assembly row
##   named after the stem of -o (version 0.0.0.0, HashAlgId SHA1 0x8004, no
##   public key) and the Module row named after the output file;
## - without references, msil-ld's built-in table (5.11.7, M21; M20's BCL
##   stand-in before it): the trailer's members and every msil.bcl
##   reference become '[mscorlib]' 4.0.0.0 b77a5c561934e089 (D10), and no
##   placeholder survives: no msil.extern, msil.bcl, msil.link or
##   msil.unresolved scope, no '<msil>Symbols', '<msil>FnAddr' or
##   '<msil>LinkInfo' type and no custom attribute (the record's carrier);
## - token sites name the output entities: a call of another object's
##   function names its MethodDef, a variable its address field, an address
##   in data the '<msil>fn_' field (one per method), a native function its
##   P/Invoke stub ('assembly', preservesig, ImplMap 0x0201, the module of the
##   import library, 5.10.11);
## - names and access (5.9.12): functions and address fields keep their
##   symbol names, GLOBAL definitions are public, LOCAL ones assembly, the
##   '<msil>fn_' fields stay private without spill classes, and the trailer
##   ('.cctor', '<msil>Main', '<msil>data', '<msil>image') is private with
##   Phase 1's flags;
## - the data image is 5.9.9's layout (a.o's segments, then b.o's, then the
##   zero part), and with at most 32 relocations '.cctor' is Phase 1's
##   straight-line sequence (5.9.10), as -S writes it for the same program;
## - row order follows input order only: the kept methods and address fields
##   by object in link order and row order, then the P/Invoke stub, then the
##   trailer's methods; TypeDef '<Module>', then '<msil>image_t'.
## The listing is the one '-S' plus ilasm gives for the same IR, up to O3's
## normalizations (5.12.6): msil-ld writes no Param rows and never sets
## InitLocals, and binds puts from the import library instead of D14's
## ucrtbase.

# REQUIRES: llvm-cil-dump
# RUN: rm -rf %t && split-file %s %t && cd %t
# RUN: llc -filetype=obj a.ll -o a.o
# RUN: llc -filetype=obj b.ll -o b.o
# RUN: llvm-lib /machine:x64 /def:%S/Inputs/native/ucrt-stdio.def /out:ucrt.lib

# DEFINE: %{none} = --implicit-check-not=msil.extern --implicit-check-not=msil.bcl \
# DEFINE:   --implicit-check-not=msil.link --implicit-check-not=msil.unresolved \
# DEFINE:   --implicit-check-not='<msil>Symbols' --implicit-check-not='<msil>FnAddr' \
# DEFINE:   --implicit-check-not='<msil>LinkInfo' --implicit-check-not=.custom

# RUN: msil-ld a.o b.o ucrt.lib -o prog.exe 2>&1 | count 0
# RUN: llvm-cil-dump prog.exe > prog.txt
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=CANON %{none} --input-file=prog.txt
# RUN: llvm-cil-dump --headers prog.exe | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=HEADERS
# RUN: llvm-cil-dump --tables prog.exe > tables.txt
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=TABLES %{none} --implicit-check-not='Table: CustomAttribute' \
# RUN:   --implicit-check-not='Table: Param ' --input-file=tables.txt

# CANON:      {{^}}pe PE32+ machine=0x8664 exe subsystem=3{{$}}
# CANON-NEXT: {{^}}cor flags=0x00000001 runtime=2.5 metadata-version=v4.0.30319{{$}}
# CANON-NEXT: {{^}}entrypoint int32(string[]) '<Module>'::'<msil>Main'{{$}}
# CANON-NEXT: {{^}}assembly 'prog' ver 0.0.0.0 flags=0x00000000 hash=0x00008004 culture='' key=-{{$}}
# CANON-NEXT: {{^}}module 'prog.exe'{{$}}
# CANON-NEXT: {{^}}assemblyref 'mscorlib' ver 4.0.0.0 flags=0x00000000 key=B7 7A 5C 56 19 34 E0 89 culture=''{{$}}
# CANON-NEXT: {{^}}moduleref 'api-ms-win-crt-stdio-l1-1-0.dll'{{$}}
# CANON-EMPTY:
# CANON-NEXT: {{^}}.class '<Module>' flags=0x00000000{{$}}
# CANON-NEXT: {{^}}  .field '<msil>data' native int flags=0x0031{{$}}
# CANON-NEXT: {{^}}  .field '<msil>fn_add3' native int flags=0x0031{{$}}
# CANON-NEXT: {{^}}  .field '<msil>image' valuetype '<msil>image_t' flags=0x0111{{$}}
# CANON-NEXT: {{^}}    .data 20 bytes{{$}}
# CANON-NEXT: {{^}}      68 65 6C 6C 6F 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 05 00 00 00{{$}}
# CANON-NEXT: {{^}}  .field 'counter' native int flags=0x0036{{$}}
# CANON-NEXT: {{^}}  .field 'msg' native int flags=0x0033{{$}}
# CANON-NEXT: {{^}}  .field 'scratch' native int flags=0x0036{{$}}
# CANON-NEXT: {{^}}  .field 'table' native int flags=0x0036{{$}}
# CANON-NEXT: {{^}}  .method '.cctor' void() flags=0x1891 impl=0x0000{{$}}
# CANON-NEXT: {{^}}    .maxstack 3{{$}}
# CANON-NEXT: {{^}}    L0: ldc.i4.s 47{{$}}
# CANON-NEXT: {{^}}    L1: conv.i{{$}}
# CANON-NEXT: {{^}}    L2: call native int(native int) [mscorlib]System.Runtime.InteropServices.Marshal::'AllocHGlobal'{{$}}
# CANON-NEXT: {{^}}    L3: ldc.i4.s 15{{$}}
# CANON-NEXT: {{^}}    L4: conv.i{{$}}
# CANON-NEXT: {{^}}    L5: add{{$}}
# CANON-NEXT: {{^}}    L6: ldc.i4.s -16{{$}}
# CANON-NEXT: {{^}}    L7: conv.i{{$}}
# CANON-NEXT: {{^}}    L8: and{{$}}
# CANON-NEXT: {{^}}    L9: stsfld native int '<Module>'::'<msil>data'{{$}}
# CANON-NEXT: {{^}}    L10: ldsfld native int '<Module>'::'<msil>data'{{$}}
# CANON-NEXT: {{^}}    L11: ldsflda valuetype '<msil>image_t' '<Module>'::'<msil>image'{{$}}
# CANON-NEXT: {{^}}    L12: ldc.i4.s 20{{$}}
# CANON-NEXT: {{^}}    L13: cpblk{{$}}
# CANON-NEXT: {{^}}    L14: ldsfld native int '<Module>'::'<msil>data'{{$}}
# CANON-NEXT: {{^}}    L15: ldc.i4.s 20{{$}}
# CANON-NEXT: {{^}}    L16: add{{$}}
# CANON-NEXT: {{^}}    L17: ldc.i4.0{{$}}
# CANON-NEXT: {{^}}    L18: ldc.i4.s 12{{$}}
# CANON-NEXT: {{^}}    L19: unaligned. 4{{$}}
# CANON-NEXT: {{^}}    L20: initblk{{$}}
# CANON-NEXT: {{^}}    L21: ldsfld native int '<Module>'::'<msil>data'{{$}}
# CANON-NEXT: {{^}}    L22: stsfld native int '<Module>'::'msg'{{$}}
# CANON-NEXT: {{^}}    L23: ldsfld native int '<Module>'::'<msil>data'{{$}}
# CANON-NEXT: {{^}}    L24: ldc.i4.8{{$}}
# CANON-NEXT: {{^}}    L25: add{{$}}
# CANON-NEXT: {{^}}    L26: stsfld native int '<Module>'::'table'{{$}}
# CANON-NEXT: {{^}}    L27: ldsfld native int '<Module>'::'<msil>data'{{$}}
# CANON-NEXT: {{^}}    L28: ldc.i4.s 16{{$}}
# CANON-NEXT: {{^}}    L29: add{{$}}
# CANON-NEXT: {{^}}    L30: stsfld native int '<Module>'::'counter'{{$}}
# CANON-NEXT: {{^}}    L31: ldsfld native int '<Module>'::'<msil>data'{{$}}
# CANON-NEXT: {{^}}    L32: ldc.i4.s 20{{$}}
# CANON-NEXT: {{^}}    L33: add{{$}}
# CANON-NEXT: {{^}}    L34: stsfld native int '<Module>'::'scratch'{{$}}
# CANON-NEXT: {{^}}    L35: ldftn int32(int32) '<Module>'::'add3'{{$}}
# CANON-NEXT: {{^}}    L36: stsfld native int '<Module>'::'<msil>fn_add3'{{$}}
# CANON-NEXT: {{^}}    L37: ldsfld native int '<Module>'::'<msil>data'{{$}}
# CANON-NEXT: {{^}}    L38: ldc.i4.8{{$}}
# CANON-NEXT: {{^}}    L39: add{{$}}
# CANON-NEXT: {{^}}    L40: ldsfld native int '<Module>'::'<msil>fn_add3'{{$}}
